      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850 to 1000 mg per dose. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg to 850 mg PO two or three times daily**, if you're starting or titrating\n- **1700 mg total per day**, divided into two or three doses\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it was confirmed. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
